.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-clean-disk
command frees up disk space by optionally removing cached package
files and cleaning port/package directories in build-from-source
package managers.  It then optionally zeros all free disk space,
which allows virtual disks to be better compressed.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-clean-disk
.ad
.fi

